# Build context for the API image.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs requirements.txt, app/ and sql/, but everything
# else in this directory still gets uploaded to the daemon on every build - a
# local .venv alone is hundreds of megabytes and invalidates nothing useful.
#
# Deny by default, then re-admit exactly what the image needs. That way a file
# added later (a .env, a dump, a notebook full of credentials) cannot end up in
# the context by accident.
*

!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!app/
!sql/
!alembic.ini
!alembic/

# Re-exclude the noise inside the admitted directories: negation patterns do
# not recurse into what a later rule re-excludes, so these must come last.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/tests/
